{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792479697,"nonce":"vH1rW6J4bdcO/K/b7ioy8yaW9do=","title":"TypeScript: native static frontend and differential conformance baseline","message":"Add the zyntax_ts frontend and zynode binary, using pinned Oxc parsing and the shared TypedProgram/HIR pipeline. Begin with strict static primitives, functions, control flow and fixed-layout reference objects. Keep TypeScript-compatible checking and an explicit opt-in soundness policy separate. Run interpreter-first with automatic release/drop insertion and Collector::None; verify aliases, borrows and caller-owned returns against Rayzor insert_free principles.\n\nBuild a reference-backed conformance harness that distinguishes acceptance, type diagnostics, runtime output, unsupported features, expected failures and unexpected passes. Reference TypeScript and Node are development tools only; native execution does not emit or execute browser JavaScript. Include a route for upstream TypeScript conformance cases and reproducible compiler versions. Unsupported language features are tracked implementation gaps, not permanent restrictions.\n\nThe broader language and dynamic JavaScript runtime are subsequent work. This focused issue closes only when the initial native implementation and harness are executable, tested and committed.","files":null}]}